{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>How many</b> — according to its plain sense, many. Or from the derivation of על כל רב ביתו (Genesis 45:8), and all of them as a sign of Your wisdom." "And the meaning of <b>the earth is full of Your possessions</b> — for there is no empty place in the earth. After he mentioned the creatures on earth, he mentioned the creatures in the sea." "And the meaning of <b>this</b> — behold, it is known and seen to be great in its size." "<b>And broad of hands</b> — its place is broad."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 104, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:16.400754354Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}